hey it's betsy from tasty and today i'm  going to tell you about one of my recipe  videos that i didn't expect to go viral  my cinnamon sugar donut cones  i don't want to discourage anyone from  making these but tears were shed behind  the scenes while filming this  i was inspired by these really cool  hungarian chimney cakes the dough is  wrapped around a stick and then baked  over an open fire so i really wanted to  transform this into something that  people could easily make at home and  then up the indulgence factor by coating  the inside with chocolate and topping it  off with some ice cream  making the dough for the cones was the  easy part  but when it came time to wrap the dough  around the aluminum foil and bake the  cones i was like why is the world  against me right now  i kept saying to myself please stay  together don't fall over  don't unravel  all of those things kind of happened  you might not know this but tasty  producers are responsible for cooking  and shooting at the same time so when  you throw food especially ice cream into  the mix things can get a little out of  control sometimes there was chocolate  and ice cream all over my hands all over  the table  cinnamon sugar and rainbow sprinkles all  over the floor  i was just like getting so frustrated  then i thought it would be a great idea  to coat the inside of the cone with  chocolate big mistake i was just worried  that the cones and assembly process  weren't going to look easy and clean  enough to really appeal to our fans i'm  a perfectionist okay there i said it for  this recipe one day of shooting turned  into three days of shooting i almost  lost it i think because i felt  disappointed behind the scenes i thought  the audience would also be disappointed  but i was wrong sometimes there's beauty  in disaster because to my surprise the  recipe was a huge hit on the internet  when i saw this video surpass 30 million  views on facebook i was like  no way  you gotta love those silver linings here  are a couple quick tips if you want to  make these when you're wrapping the  dough around the aluminum foil you  almost want to slightly overlap the  dough you want to make sure that the  seams are sealed and the ends are tucked  in  otherwise the cone could unravel during  baking be very careful when transferring  your cones to the oven the higher walls  of the muffin tin help keep your cones  upright but a couple of mine did topple  over so just keep an eye on them  anyway have fun with it these cones  really are so good i can't thank you  enough for all your support and i can't  wait to make more recipes for you  oh yes  you
 

